Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> I am observing the csaiph bots on NAO. (Very impressive speed, BTW.)
> But I am wondering about the tactics; why do they ignore all scrolls
> potions and wands? Even if one doesn't use them, I find it very risky
> to let them there for use by monsters. Csaiph seems to be focussed on
> melee and ranged missile combat only?

I suspect saiph simply doesn't know how to use them. (This is a common
problem with bots; in terms of the other bot, TAEB, TAEB::AI::Behavioral
knows about wands, but not scrolls or potions, and TAEB::AI::Planar
doesn't know about any of those items.) Writing a NetHack bot is
surprisingly difficult, and just getting the basics working is a higher
priority than implementing item use.

I seem to remember an older version of saiph (or a planned future
version?) used to empty wands it found lying around then discard them,
in order to stop monsters using them against it. That's probably
suboptimal compared to knowing when to use them and what they do,
though, and there'd be a risk of the wands bouncing, or of create
monster, without the bot knowing how the wands actually worked.

